13.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A

The canonical attenuation model continues to single out A as the sole mutation that directly prevents 3-4 terminator assembly itself. Under high-Trp conditions the ribosome normally covers region 2, leaving 3 free to pair with 4. When 1-2 pairing is blocked, however, region 2 remains single-stranded long enough for the nascent region 3 to nucleate the competing 2-3 antiterminator at the moment region 3 is transcribed; this kinetic preemption sequesters the sequences required for the 3-4 stem-loop before region 4 can ever compete. Consequently read-through occurs regardless of tryptophan level.  

Option C, by contrast, leaves the 3-4 hairpin nucleotides and their folding pathway unchanged; it only alters the downstream U-run that follows an already-formed stem-loop, so the structural decision favoring termination is preserved. B would actually stabilize 3-4 pairing, while D and E act outside the hairpin competition altogether. The mutually exclusive hairpin logic therefore remains unambiguous: only A satisfies the question’s explicit requirement that formation of the 3-4 terminator be prevented under repressing conditions.}

